                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Horse game from the golden era of said games, so naturally I recommend this game to fellow enthusiasts of the era. In saying that;\r\n\r\nTHE GOOD:\r\nPretty setup, graphics have aged well enough, overall aesthetic is unmistakable and iconic. Captures a feeling from the era many struggle with. Feels like opening a British book from 1999 for young kids learning to ride a horse, the sort with more information than needed for dream-fuel purposes. Character and horse models are both well enough aged, animations are better than you'd expect.\r\n\r\nTHE BAD:\r\nGameplay loop is ass (you could have expected this). Grinding, lots of those \"horse care\" mini-games people assume you'll love. Point of the game is to reach 4 stars, to do so you need to uphold a ridiculous degree of grind each in game day. Makes more sense to grind to 4 star, then after you've unlocked everything let the rating fall back and play as you'd like. In game you have from 8am - 6pm to grind, which chews up very quickly. The racing is basic as basic comes. Controls are okay.\r\n\r\nI recommend, instead of this game, Petz Horsez 2 for those after the aesthetic. For those after the gameplay, Lucinda Greens Equestrian Challenge (which IIRC, is now abandonware but can be downloaded online for free thanks to dedicated archivists).\r\n\r\nPH2 perfectly encapsulates the 2000s Equestrian ideal aesthetically and whilst it is visibly much older it has still held up well. It is also much more in depth than this game in all areas and follows the same basic concept, minus a guest system.\r\n\r\nLGEQ is a fantastic eventing simulator for the era. It does have some flaws here and there, and I'm positive a handful of jumps on the 3* and 4* courses are backwards, but it has the same general feel with much more fleshed out mechanics and progression. Much less heavy grind (this game, you might spend 5 minutes IRL patting a horse to uphold a star standard. LGEQ you'll spend about 3). Graphically it is about on par with MRS:LwH, though the environments are not so beautiful.\r\n\r\nTLDR; Yes, play it, but you'll be bored quickly :)\r\n\r\n",
